{
  "Small badge beside the product name; labels this page as an interactive demo/sandbox, not a children's playground\u0004playground": "démo",
  "Tooltip on a status dot. 'isReady()' is an API name — keep it verbatim. 'gate UI on this' = show the UI only once it is ready; 'flash-of-untranslated-content' is the technical term for untranslated text briefly showing (FOUC)\u0004isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content": "isReady() — conditionner l'affichage de l'interface utilisateur à cet état pour éviter le flash de contenu non traduit",
  "ready": "prêt",
  "loading…": "chargement…",
  "Heading above the sidebar table-of-contents navigation links\u0004On this page": "Sur cette page",
  "Hero tagline (marketing register). 'Angular' is the framework name and 'i18n' the abbreviation for internationalization — keep both. 'signal-first' means built around Angular Signals; render the technical sense, not 'first signal'\u0004Angular i18n, the signal-first way": "i18n Angular, l'approche signal-first",
  "Hero subheading (marketing prose). Keep the product/tech names verbatim: 'ng-linguo', 'Angular', 'SignalStore', 'HTML'. 'signals'/'store methods' are Angular Signals concepts; 'reads'/'writes' are data access, not literal reading/writing\u0004ng-linguo is a complete internationalization solution for Angular built on a SignalStore. Reads are signals, writes are store methods, and translators never see a line of HTML. Flip the language switcher above and watch every example below re-render reactively.": "ng-linguo est une solution d'internationalisation complète pour Angular, basée sur un SignalStore. Les lectures sont des signaux, les écritures sont des méthodes de store, et les traducteurs ne voient jamais une ligne de HTML. Basculez le sélecteur de langue ci-dessus et observez chaque exemple ci-dessous se re-rendre de manière réactive.",
  "Section heading: initial setup / installation of the library\u0004Setup": "Configuration",
  "Card title. 'store' = the ng-linguo SignalStore (a noun); 'Bootstrap' = set up / initialize\u0004Bootstrap the store": "Amorcer le store",
  "Card body (developer-docs tone). Keep API names verbatim: provideTranslate(), restoreLang(). 'store' = the SignalStore; 'loads' = fetches translations; 'Dictionaries' = the JSON translation files; 'keyed by source string' = the English text is the lookup key\u0004provideTranslate() wires up the store; it never loads automatically — restoreLang() is the explicit kick-off. Dictionaries are plain JSON keyed by source string.": "provideTranslate() connecte le store ; il ne se charge jamais automatiquement — restoreLang() est le déclenchement explicite. Les dictionnaires sont des fichiers JSON simples, indexés par la chaîne source.",
  "Section heading. 'pipe' is the Angular template-pipe concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol 't'\u0004The [code]t[/code] pipe": "Le pipe [code]t[/code]",
  "Card title. 'template' = the Angular HTML template\u0004Translate in the template": "Traduire dans le template",
  "Card body. 'key' = the lookup key; 'falls through to the source' = shows the original English when no translation exists; 'blank' = empty\u0004The source English string is the key. With no translation it falls through to the source, so the UI is never blank.": "La chaîne source anglaise est la clé. Sans traduction, elle revient à la source, ainsi l'interface utilisateur n'est jamais vide.",
  "He was driving incredibly fast!": "Il conduisait incroyablement vite !",
  "Section heading. 'directive' is the Angular directive concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol '[t]'\u0004The [code][[t][/code] directive": "La directive [code][[t][/code]",
  "Card title. 'element' = an HTML / DOM element\u0004Translate an element": "Traduire un élément",
  "Card body. 'signals' = Angular Signals; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file; 'directive' = the Angular [t] directive; 'subscription bookkeeping' = manually managing RxJS subscriptions\u0004Reads through to the store's signals — once a dictionary loads, the directive re-renders with no subscription bookkeeping.": "Accède aux signaux du store — une fois qu'un dictionnaire est chargé, la directive se re-rend sans gestion manuelle des abonnements.",
  "Card title. 'TypeScript' is the programming language name — keep verbatim\u0004Translate in TypeScript": "Traduire en TypeScript",
  "Card body. 'the pipe' = the Angular t pipe; 'component code' = TypeScript class code; keep computed() verbatim; 'params' = the ICU parameters; 'reactive' = updates automatically\u0004The pipe's counterpart for component code. Read it inside a computed() and it stays reactive to both params and the active language.": "L'équivalent du pipe pour le code de composant. Lisez-le à l'intérieur d'un computed() et il reste réactif aux paramètres et à la langue active.",
  "Section heading: grammatical plural forms (one file / many files)\u0004Plurals": "Pluriels",
  "Card title. 'Cardinal plurals' = counting forms (1 file / 2 files), as opposed to ordinals\u0004Cardinal plurals across languages": "Pluriels cardinaux dans différentes langues",
  "Card body. EN/PL = English/Polish; one/few/many/other are CLDR plural-category names — keep them in English; 'count' is a variable name (keep); 'category switch' = the plural form changing\u0004EN has one/other; PL has one/few/many/other; an exact 0 variant reads better than '0'. Walk count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to see the category switch.": "L'anglais utilise one/other ; le polonais utilise one/few/many/other ; une variante exacte pour 0 est plus lisible que '0'. Faites varier le compteur (count) à 1, 2, 5, 22 en polonais pour observer le changement de catégorie.",
  "Section heading: ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …), not cardinal counts\u0004Ordinals": "Ordinaux",
  "Card title. 'Ordinal' = ranking forms (1st/2nd/3rd); 'categories' = the CLDR plural categories\u0004Ordinal categories": "Catégories ordinales",
  "Card body. st/nd/rd/th are the English ordinal suffixes; one/two/few/other are CLDR category names (keep in English); EN/PL/DE = English/Polish/German; '{n}.' shows the number followed by a period\u0004EN uses st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other); PL and DE collapse to a plain '{n}.'.": "L'anglais utilise st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other) ; le polonais et l'allemand se réduisent à un simple '{n}.'.",
  "Section heading. 'select' is the ICU MessageFormat 'select' construct (pick a variant by gender) — not a dropdown and not the verb 'to select'\u0004Gender select": "Sélection par genre",
  "Card title. 'Select' = the ICU select construct (choose a variant by value), not a dropdown; 'a string' = a text value\u0004Select on a string": "Sélectionner sur une chaîne",
  "Card body. 'pronoun' = he/she/they; 'gendered past-tense verb' = a verb form that changes with gender (as in Polish); 'count × gender' = the combination of both; 'cross-product' = every combination\u0004EN swaps the pronoun; PL swaps the gendered past-tense verb. The second line combines count × gender — a cross-product that differs per language.": "L'anglais change le pronom ; le polonais change le verbe au passé genré. La deuxième ligne combine le nombre × le genre — un produit croisé qui diffère selon les langues.",
  "Section heading: locale-aware number formatting (digit-group separators)\u0004Number formatting": "Formatage des nombres",
  "Card title. 'grouping' = digit-group separators in numbers (1,000 vs 1.000 vs 1 000); 'Locale-aware' = follows the active language\u0004Locale-aware grouping": "Regroupement sensible à la locale",
  "Card body. ':number' is an ICU formatter token (keep verbatim); en/de/pl = English/German/Polish; the figures show how each locale groups digits\u0004The :number formatter follows the active locale: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.": "Le formateur :number suit la locale active : en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.",
  "Section heading. 'Context' = the translation disambiguation feature (gettext msgctxt); 'homonyms' = words spelled the same but meaning different things\u0004Context (homonyms)": "Contexte (homonymes)",
  "Card title about homonyms / disambiguation\u0004Same word, different meaning": "Même mot, sens différent",
  "Card body. 'context' is the ng-linguo option name (keep verbatim); 'key' = lookup key; 'gettext msgctxt' is a technical term (keep); 'note for translators' = a hint; 'sense' = meaning\u0004context is part of the key (gettext msgctxt) and doubles as a note for translators. Switch to Polish to see each sense diverge.": "context fait partie de la clé (gettext msgctxt) et sert également de note pour les traducteurs. Passez au polonais pour voir chaque sens diverger.",
  "audio player\u0004Play": "Lecture",
  "game\u0004Play": "Jouer",
  "direction\u0004Right": "Droite",
  "correct\u0004Right": "Juste",
  "sequence\u0004Order": "Ordre",
  "purchase\u0004Order": "Commande",
  "no cost\u0004Free": "Gratuit",
  "available\u0004Free": "Libre",
  "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations\u0004Rich text (slot tags)": "Texte enrichi (balises de slot)",
  "Card title. 'emphasis' = bold/italic styling; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file. The point: no HTML appears in translation files\u0004Links and emphasis without HTML in the dictionary": "Liens et mise en évidence sans HTML dans le dictionnaire",
  "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'literal bracket' = a real [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep); 'zero by construction' = impossible by design. [[name] shows an escaped literal bracket — keep the doubled brackets\u0004Translators see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — each binds to your own ng-template tFor, with no predefined HTML. Need a literal bracket in your prose? Double the opening one. Translator content is never inserted as HTML; XSS surface is zero by construction.": "Les traducteurs voient des slots nommés comme [[name]…[[/name] — chacun se lie à votre propre ng-template tFor, sans HTML prédéfini. Besoin d'un crochet littéral dans votre texte ? Doublez le crochet ouvrant. Le contenu du traducteur n'est jamais inséré comme HTML ; la surface d'attaque XSS est nulle par construction.",
  "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it\u0004Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started": "Lisez la [docs]documentation[/docs] pour commencer",
  "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]": "En continuant, vous acceptez nos [terms]Conditions d'utilisation[/terms]",
  "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'\u0004[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone": "[warn]Attention :[/warn] cette action est irréversible",
  "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly\u0004Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot": "[[b]bold[[/b] échappé reste littéral — [b]ceci[/b] est un slot",
  "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]": "Acceptez nos [link]Conditions [b]Générales[/b][/link]",
  "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)\u0004ESLint & a11y": "ESLint et a11y",
  "Card title (colloquial). 'linter' = ESLint; 'keep the linter happy' = satisfy the lint rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text content\u0004Keep the linter happy with empty [t] elements": "Contenter le linter avec des éléments [t] vides",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'a11y' = accessibility; 'markup' = HTML; 'fallback' = the default shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page\u0004The a11y rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content flags empty headings, anchors, and buttons. A [t] element fills its text at runtime, so the source string can move out of the markup entirely — the headings on this page are empty [t] elements; only the hero keeps its text as a fallback.": "La règle d'accessibilité @angular-eslint/template/elements-content signale les titres, ancres et boutons vides. Un élément [t] remplit son texte à l'exécution, ainsi la chaîne source peut être entièrement retirée du balisage — les titres de cette page sont des éléments [t] vides ; seul le titre principal conserve son texte comme solution de repli.",
  "Section heading: translating the app automatically using an AI / LLM\u0004Translating with AI": "Traduction avec l'IA",
  "Card title. 'source string' = the original English text; 'catalog' = the translation file (.po)\u0004From source string to translated catalog": "De la chaîne source au catalogue traduit",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator. 'catalogs' = translation files; 'chat model' = an LLM; 'merges the reply' = applies the response; 'clipboard copy/paste' = manual copying\u0004The extract CLI keeps gettext .po catalogs and compiles them to runtime JSON. Translate by copying a prompt into any chat model, or fully automatically: point translator at a module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, you keep the SDK and the API key. Omit translator and translation stays a clipboard copy/paste.": "L'interface de ligne de commande (CLI) extract gère les catalogues gettext .po et les compile en JSON pour l'exécution. Traduisez en copiant une invite dans n'importe quel modèle de chat, ou de manière entièrement automatique : dirigez translator vers un module qui appelle votre propre fournisseur d'IA — ng-linguo écrit l'invite et fusionne la réponse, vous conservez le SDK et la clé API. Omettez translator et la traduction reste un copier-coller manuel.",
  "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo\u0004Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.": "Construit avec ng-linguo · ce bac à sable est aussi une documentation vivante.",
